{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 + avgpool (config_005, acc=0.650) and pca_n2000 + avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) show that the RNA encoder choice contributes ~6 points of accuracy in the multiprofile setting. Aggregation method (avgpool vs transformer) has negligible effect (0.650 vs 0.653). scgpt is the only untested RNA encoder. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as an RNA encoder in the best-performing multiprofile setting? config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), isolating encoder quality. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in multimodal or image-encoder experiments, we need to know the ceiling of the RNA-only pipeline. If scgpt substantially beats scvi_n200, it changes which RNA encoder to pair with image in multimodal configs; if it underperforms, we can confidently anchor multimodal experiments on scvi_n200. This reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design axis (representation) with minimal confounds."
}

